<Project>
  <!-- Single version for the whole repo; milestones bump it (plan §7).
       0.11.0 is RELEASED (its contents: CHANGELOG [0.11.0] - M39 agent tokens and
       the caller-contract collapse). 0.12.0 is RELEASED (its contents: CHANGELOG
       [0.12.0] - the M42 package splits that moved OAuth, LoginExchange, Hmac,
       Operations, caller keys and agent tokens out of the core into their own
       packages (ADR-0005); publishing itself is the separate maintainer ceremony
       in PUBLISHING.md). 0.13.0 is RELEASED (its contents: CHANGELOG [0.13.0] -
       the caller-key rotation fix, the health switch that is really off, and
       ADR-0006's replace/turn-off contract). This line carries `0.13.1`, the
       release number set by the 0.13.1 release prep — a release-candidate number,
       deliberately not a development line; it reopens as `0.14.0-dev` (the M45
       line) only in the post-publish step below.
       The -dev suffix is load-bearing: candidate packs carry a prerelease
       version, so they can never collide in the machine-wide NuGet cache with a
       published version (slice-4b hazard F3). A released number without -dev
       does collide by design — measured during the 0.12.0 development window:
       candidate packs came out labelled CredProx.0.12.0 and the machine cache
       held unreleased bytes under the released version id, so anything that
       resolves by version alone could take dev bytes for the release. Right
       after publishing, evict the exact-version cache and reopen this line as
       <next>-dev; both steps live in PUBLISHING.md's post-publish step.
       Two importers, deliberately kept in sync by import: the root
       Directory.Build.props (every library and the samples) and the hermetic
       tools/m33-soak/SoakHost props — the soak host tracks this number without
       inheriting the library's build policy. -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Version>0.13.1</Version>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
